<section class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 py-16">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-6 text-center">How to Download Facebook Videos (Public & Private)</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 text-center mb-10">Last updated: <%= currentYear %></p>

    <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        Facebook is one of the most popular platforms for sharing videos, live streams, and reels. Whether you want to save a public cooking tutorial, your own live stream, or a friend's public video, this guide explains how to do it safely and legally.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Public Facebook videos vs. private videos</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400"><strong>Public videos</strong> can be viewed by anyone and are the easiest to download. <strong>Private videos</strong> or friends-only videos require you to be logged in and have permission to view them. Downloading private content you do not own or have rights to may violate Facebook's Terms and copyright law.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">How to download a public Facebook video</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        <li>Open the Facebook video in your browser or app.</li>
        <li>Tap the <strong>Share</strong> button and choose <strong>Copy link</strong>.</li>
        <li>Go to <a href="/" class="text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400 hover:underline"><%= siteTitle %></a>.</li>
        <li>Paste the URL, solve the captcha, and click <strong>Get Video</strong>.</li>
        <li>Pick an MP4 format and click to download.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Private or friends-only videos</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">If you own the video or the owner has given you permission, you may need to provide your Facebook cookies. In the Advanced options, paste your browser cookies so the server can access the private page. Do not share your cookies with anyone else.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Legal and safety tips</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        <li>Only download videos you created or have permission to save.</li>
        <li>Do not redistribute other people's private content.</li>
        <li>Respect Facebook's Terms of Service and local copyright laws.</li>
        <li>Keep your cookies secure and delete them after use.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <details class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 p-4">
          <summary class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white cursor-pointer">Can I download Facebook Live videos?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm">Yes, if the live video has been published as a replay and is public or you have permission.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 p-4">
          <summary class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white cursor-pointer">Why does Facebook block some downloads?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm">Facebook may block cloud server IPs. Try using cookies or a residential/proxy IP.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 p-4">
          <summary class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white cursor-pointer">Is downloading Facebook videos legal?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm">Only if you own the content or have permission. Public content does not automatically mean it is copyright-free.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
